1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,141
Your AI can write code.

2
00:00:02,091 --> 00:00:04,557
But does it have the right context?

3
00:00:04,557 --> 00:00:09,375
When every task starts with another tour of your repository, the real work has to wait.

4
00:00:11,142 --> 00:00:12,921
Meet CodeAtlas.

5
00:00:12,871 --> 00:00:19,223
An open source AI context engine that turns your TypeScript and JavaScript project into a reusable, searchable map.

6
00:00:20,975 --> 00:00:22,789
Scan the source.

7
00:00:22,739 --> 00:00:25,250
Connect symbols and dependencies.

8
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:27,614
Keep the index on your machine.

9
00:00:27,614 --> 00:00:31,705
When code changes, update the map instead of starting from scratch.

10
00:00:33,475 --> 00:00:35,402
Search for a symbol.

11
00:00:35,352 --> 00:00:37,227
Inspect its source.

12
00:00:37,227 --> 00:00:41,977
Build a focused context package for the task, with an explicit token budget.

13
00:00:41,977 --> 00:00:44,659
Give your tools evidence they can work with.

14
00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:50,656
Export context for your coding tools, or connect through MCP.

15
00:00:50,606 --> 00:00:54,845
Here is a real OpenCode response on a small authentication example.

16
00:00:54,845 --> 00:00:57,379
CodeAtlas prepares the context.

17
00:00:57,379 --> 00:00:59,640
Your agent does the reasoning.

18
00:01:01,433 --> 00:01:03,531
Go beyond one prompt.

19
00:01:03,481 --> 00:01:08,970
Thirteen built in Skills bring reusable instructions for debugging, research, and development.

20
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:12,492
Discover optional tools, then choose what to install.

21
00:01:14,267 --> 00:01:16,114
Local indexing.

22
00:01:16,064 --> 00:01:18,098
Deterministic search.

23
00:01:18,098 --> 00:01:20,371
Optional AI enrichment.

24
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:24,223
The audited build passes thirteen hundred and ninety four tests.

25
00:01:24,223 --> 00:01:28,201
Explore the developer preview, and help shape what comes next.

